    "https://jobs.nmu.edu/jobs/earth-environmental-and-geographical-sciences-assistant-professor-in-environmental-hazards-tenure-track-marquette-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track",
      "description": "Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track - Marquette, Michigan, United States Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track - Marquette, Michigan, United States Skip to Main Content Northern Michigan University Careers Kiosk mode Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track 495188 Marquette, Michigan, 49855 Earth, Env, & Geog Sciences Faculty and Librarians Closing on: Nov 22 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track Department: Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences Term of Assignment: Tenure Track Term End Date, If Applicable: FLSA Status: Exempt = not eligible for overtime Salary: Competitive Travel: Less than 10% Brief Statement of Duties Brief Statement of Duties: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses that complement and strengthen the Department’s curriculum, maintain an active and student-engaged research program in environmental hazards and applied GIS or a closely related field, publish in peer-reviewed outlets, and pursue external funding opportunities. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate and graduate students and contributing to departmental, university, and professional service. This position is not available for sponsorship. This is a campus-based position. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Doctorate or equivalent terminal degree Discipline/Degree Area: Environmental Hazards, Geoscience, Environmental Science, or a closely related field Required Specialized Training/Certifications: Ph.D. degree in Environmental Hazards, Geoscience, Environmental Science, or a closely related field granted by August 15, 2027. Required Minimum Work Experience: Required minimum qualifications include a Ph.D. degree in Environmental Hazards, Geoscience, Environmental Science, or a closely related field granted by August 15, 2027. Evidence of an active scholarly agenda; a publication record in related disciplines; demonstrated university teaching experience with a strong commitment to high-quality undergraduate and graduate instruction and advising. Experience with applied research methods, including field-based GIS methods, is required. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, or Attributes Required for Satisfactory Performance of the Position Duties: We seek a candidate with demonstrated experience in undergraduate teaching, advising, and student engagement in research. Successful candidates will be capable of teaching GC 210 Earth Hazards, GC 475 Environmental Impact Assessment, GC 335 Geographic Information Systems, and upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Additional desirable courses this candidate could teach include GC 428 Spatial Analysis, GC 425 Remote Sensing, GC 482 Earth Systems Interactions, or a new course that integrates environmental science, geospatial analysis, risk assessment, hazard mitigation planning, and/or remediation. Successful candidates will have demonstrated teaching and applied research experience related to environmental hazards such as wildfires, flooding, drought, earthquakes, landslides, brownfield remediation, or sea/lake level rise. The successful applicant will demonstrate the ability to produce environmental hazards scholarship and contribute to collaborative research initiatives. Additional Desirable Qualifications Additional Desirable Qualifications: Experience securing external grants, leading field-based applied research activities, demonstrated excellence in undergraduate teaching, advising and student engagement in research, interest in collaborative and interdisciplinary projects with existing faculty that examine human–environment interactions, resource management, or sustainability challenges, and experience integrating geographic information systems or remote sensing in environmental hazards research and instruction. Desirable qualifications include candidates who have experience with professional risk assessment, hazard mitigation planning, and remediation. We seek a broadly trained environmental hazards scientist with professional experience contributing to environmental impact assessments and integrating social dimensions of environmental hazards. Other Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicant materials will include a faculty application, cover letter, CV/Resume, unofficial transcripts, a teaching statement, a research statement, and mentorship statement. You may upload your mentorship statement with either your research or teaching statement. Contact Information: Matt Van Grinsven, Chair - mvangrin@nmu.edu NMU is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now! Recently Posted Jobs Economics/Assistant Professor/Three Year Term Economics Teach courses in Money and Banking, Intermediate Macroeconomics, Principles of Macroeconomics, and be prepared to teach Introduction to Economics and Principles of Microeconomics. The normal teaching load is three courses (12 credit hours) per semester, with up to three different course preparations per semester. Additional responsibilities include service at the department, college, and university levels, and student advising. Resources are available for engaging in professional development, research, and conference travel. Desirable qualifications: Being able to teach Comparative Economic Systems and American Economic History. Being able to integrate emerging technologies, including AI, into teaching and other professional activities in innovative and effective ways. This position is campus-based and is not currently eligible for sponsorship. Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track Earth, Env, & Geog Sciences The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses that complement and strengthen the Department’s curriculum, maintain an active and student-engaged research program in environmental hazards and applied GIS or a closely related field, publish in peer-reviewed outlets, and pursue external funding opportunities. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate and graduate students and contributing to departmental, university, and professional service. This position is not available for sponsorship. This is a campus-based position. Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services Controllers Office Plan, develop and refine operating procedures and computerized systems for financial reporting. Monitor, review and document University financial transactions for compliance with accounting principles, University policies, federal circulars and Internal Revenue Service rules and regulations. Prepare and/or assist with preparation of many of the University's financial statements, annual audits, income tax return, revenue projections of University endowments and expenditure projections for special projects. Responsible for all post award financial management functions, including expenditure monitoring, financial reporting, grant close-out, and audit. Biology - Forensics/Assistant Professor/Tenure Track Biology The Tenure Track Assistant Professor position requires a Ph.D. in forensic biology or a related field. Ph.D must be earned by August 15, 2027. The assignments will include teaching a range of courses related to forensic science such as Introduction to Forensic Science, Forensic Biology, Forensic Microscopy, Forensic Entomology, other areas of forensic science, a career seminar, or advanced courses in areas of specialty. Assignments may also include teaching in related fields including human anatomy & physiology. The selected candidate will be expected to develop a research program in forensic biology incorporating undergraduate and graduate students. Preference will be given to those applicants whose work engages decomposition ecology or related specialties in entomology, microbiology, morphological decomposition, and postmortem interval estimation. This is a campus based position. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Temporary Production Cook Dining Services-Central Office This is a posting for part-time temporary positions which are used to supplement and augment the regular NMU workforce. This position is primarily responsible for food preparation and cooking. The length of hire might vary from 1 day to 4 months. Philosophy/Assistant Professor/Three Year Term Philosophy Brief Statement of Duties: The course load will be 12 credits per semester, with multiple preps each term. The teaching responsibilities will include various applied ethics courses (computer, legal, medical) as well as a course in social and political philosophy. There will also be additional service responsibilities in support of the department, college, and university. The appointment will require having an active research agenda. This is a campus-based position. This position is currently not available for sponsorship. Sign up for job alerts By signing up for job alerts, you will be notified of vacancies based on your career category selection. You are able to sign up for as many career categories as you would like. Job Alert 8c1bb29b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Earth, Env, & Geog Sciences Earth, Env, & Geog Sciences Categories Faculty-College of Arts and Sciences Faculty-College of Arts and Sciences First Name (required) 474f9137 Last Name (required) 4de98272 Email (required) 5cf253e9 Phone Number 7a407115 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra