    "https://jobs.nmu.edu/jobs/manager-grant-accounting-accounting-services-marquette-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services",
      "description": "Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services - Marquette, Michigan, United States Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services - Marquette, Michigan, United States Skip to Main Content Northern Michigan University Careers Kiosk mode Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services 495183 Marquette, Michigan, 49855 Controllers Office Staff Closing on: Oct 21 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services Department: Controllers Office Term of Assignment: Continuing Term End Date, If Applicable: FLSA Status: Exempt = not eligible for overtime Work Schedule: Traditionally Monday-Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm with occasional evening and weekend work required. Salary: Targeted salary range: $68,000-$74,000 Travel: Less than 10% Brief Statement of Duties Brief Statement of Duties: Plan, develop and refine operating procedures and computerized systems for financial reporting. Monitor, review and document University financial transactions for compliance with accounting principles, University policies, federal circulars and Internal Revenue Service rules and regulations. Prepare and/or assist with preparation of many of the University's financial statements, annual audits, income tax return, revenue projections of University endowments and expenditure projections for special projects. Responsible for all post award financial management functions, including expenditure monitoring, financial reporting, grant close-out, and audit. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor's Degree Discipline/Degree Area: Required Specialized Training/Certifications: Required Minimum Work Experience: Four years of experience in accounting, auditing, or finance. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, or Attributes Required for Satisfactory Performance of the Position Duties: Current knowledge of accounting practices and principles. Oral and written communication and comprehension skills. Ability to organize, plan and prioritize work. Ability to work effectively within a team-based environment. Computer and software application skills. Current knowledge of tax laws. Additional Desirable Qualifications Additional Desirable Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Accounting, Master's Degree in Business and/or CPA certificate. Higher education fund accounting seminars and workshops. Experience in financial accounting for federal, state, and local grants. Certified Fiscal Research Administrator or comparable certification. Other Special Instructions to Applicants: Submit application, cover letter, resume and references. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Contact Information: Erica Jean, HR Generalist, 906-227-1087 NMU is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now! Recently Posted Jobs Economics/Assistant Professor/Three Year Term Economics Teach courses in Money and Banking, Intermediate Macroeconomics, Principles of Macroeconomics, and be prepared to teach Introduction to Economics and Principles of Microeconomics. The normal teaching load is three courses (12 credit hours) per semester, with up to three different course preparations per semester. Additional responsibilities include service at the department, college, and university levels, and student advising. Resources are available for engaging in professional development, research, and conference travel. Desirable qualifications: Being able to teach Comparative Economic Systems and American Economic History. Being able to integrate emerging technologies, including AI, into teaching and other professional activities in innovative and effective ways. This position is campus-based and is not currently eligible for sponsorship. Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track Earth, Env, & Geog Sciences The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses that complement and strengthen the Department’s curriculum, maintain an active and student-engaged research program in environmental hazards and applied GIS or a closely related field, publish in peer-reviewed outlets, and pursue external funding opportunities. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate and graduate students and contributing to departmental, university, and professional service. This position is not available for sponsorship. This is a campus-based position. Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services Controllers Office Plan, develop and refine operating procedures and computerized systems for financial reporting. Monitor, review and document University financial transactions for compliance with accounting principles, University policies, federal circulars and Internal Revenue Service rules and regulations. Prepare and/or assist with preparation of many of the University's financial statements, annual audits, income tax return, revenue projections of University endowments and expenditure projections for special projects. Responsible for all post award financial management functions, including expenditure monitoring, financial reporting, grant close-out, and audit. Biology - Forensics/Assistant Professor/Tenure Track Biology The Tenure Track Assistant Professor position requires a Ph.D. in forensic biology or a related field. Ph.D must be earned by August 15, 2027. The assignments will include teaching a range of courses related to forensic science such as Introduction to Forensic Science, Forensic Biology, Forensic Microscopy, Forensic Entomology, other areas of forensic science, a career seminar, or advanced courses in areas of specialty. Assignments may also include teaching in related fields including human anatomy & physiology. The selected candidate will be expected to develop a research program in forensic biology incorporating undergraduate and graduate students. Preference will be given to those applicants whose work engages decomposition ecology or related specialties in entomology, microbiology, morphological decomposition, and postmortem interval estimation. This is a campus based position. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Temporary Production Cook Dining Services-Central Office This is a posting for part-time temporary positions which are used to supplement and augment the regular NMU workforce. This position is primarily responsible for food preparation and cooking. The length of hire might vary from 1 day to 4 months. Philosophy/Assistant Professor/Three Year Term Philosophy Brief Statement of Duties: The course load will be 12 credits per semester, with multiple preps each term. The teaching responsibilities will include various applied ethics courses (computer, legal, medical) as well as a course in social and political philosophy. There will also be additional service responsibilities in support of the department, college, and university. The appointment will require having an active research agenda. This is a campus-based position. This position is currently not available for sponsorship. Sign up for job alerts By signing up for job alerts, you will be notified of vacancies based on your career category selection. You are able to sign up for as many career categories as you would like. Job Alert 086dfacb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Controllers Office Controllers Office Categories Business/Accounting/Finance/Purchasing Other Business/Accounting/Finance/Purchasing Other First Name (required) 8744d969 Last Name (required) 89232fb2 Email (required) 926ace9c Phone Number 79b1a9c5 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Austral