    "https://jobs.nmu.edu/jobs/records-management-digital-accessibility-coordinator-marquette-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator",
      "description": "Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator - Marquette, Michigan, United States Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator - Marquette, Michigan, United States Skip to Main Content Northern Michigan University Careers Kiosk mode Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator 495193 Marquette, Michigan, 49855 Internal Audit/Risk Management Staff Closing on: Nov 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator Department: Internal Audit/Risk Management Term of Assignment: Continuing Term End Date, If Applicable: FLSA Status: Exempt = not eligible for overtime Work Schedule: Traditionally Monday-Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm with occasional evening and weekend work required. Salary: Targeted salary range: $51,000-$54,400 Travel: No travel Brief Statement of Duties Brief Statement of Duties: Manage University records to ensure appropriate access, security, retention, preservation, and disposition in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, and University requirements. Support compliance with digital accessibility standards by assisting employees in creating and maintaining accessible digital records and content. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Associate's Degree Discipline/Degree Area: Required Specialized Training/Certifications: Required Minimum Work Experience: One year of progressively responsible experience in records management, information management, digital accessibility, compliance, business administration, or a related field. Experience with digital accessibility. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, or Attributes Required for Satisfactory Performance of the Position Duties: Knowledge of records management principles, practices and applicable laws and regulations governing records access, security, preservation, management, confidentiality, retention and disposition. Knowledge of digital accessibility standards and practices and their practical application across documents, spreadsheets, forms, PDFs, video, and other digital formats. Ability to apply digital accessibility standards to electronic documents and records and provide hands-on assistance to employees in creating and maintaining accessible content. Ability to exercise sound judgement and maintain strict confidentiality when handling sensitive information. Ability to partner with Information Technology personnel and other university staff to design and deliver effective small-group or one-on-one training on records management, digital accessibility, and related university policies and requirements. Ability to analyze and organize complex information. Strong oral and written communication skills. Ability to multitask. Ability to establish and maintain productive working relations with a wide variety of individuals. Ability to work independently while also contributing effectively to cross-functional teams. Ability to lift and carry materials weighing 50 pounds or more with or without reasonable accommodation. Additional Desirable Qualifications Additional Desirable Qualifications: Professional certification such as ADS, CPACC, CRM, and/or other certifications from the Institute of Certified Records Managers or ARMA International. Certification in records management or digital accessibility. Progressively responsible experience in records management, accessible content development, and/ or information management. Experience in information management compliance and best practices and knowledge of ISO 15489 Records Management principles. Experience with higher education. Other Special Instructions to Applicants: Submit application, cover letter, resume and references. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Contact Information: Erica Jean, HR Generalist, 906-227-1087 NMU is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now! Recently Posted Jobs Scene Shop Manager Theatre & Dance Responsible for managing the daily operations of the scene shop and supporting the construction and implementation of scenery for all productions within the Department of Theatre & Dance (NMU TD), inclusive of the Wildcat Performing Arts Academy (WPAA). Supervise student workers, additional hired artists, and volunteers while maintaining a safe and professional work environment, and collaborate closely with faculty, staff, and student designers to realize scenic elements for NMU TD & WPAA academic-year and summer productions. Play a vital role in training students in theatrical craftsmanship and shop safety while helping the department maintain efficient and industry-aligned production processes. Production Cook Dining Services-Northern Center Under routine supervision, provide skills and engage in the preparation of food. Prepare a wide variety of soups, salads, entrees, desserts, bakery and pastry items; use a variety of kitchen equipment; follow standardized recipe files; and make recommendations for change/improvement. Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator Internal Audit/Risk Management Manage University records to ensure appropriate access, security, retention, preservation, and disposition in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, and University requirements. Support compliance with digital accessibility standards by assisting employees in creating and maintaining accessible digital records and content. Food Service Worker II-Retail Dining Services-The Lights Under routine supervision, perform a variety of duties necessary for the daily maintenance, operation and supervision of employees in a retail operation. Provide skills and perform duties in the preparation and resale of various food, beverage and retails items. Ensure success through excellent customer service and maintenance of retail operation standards. Custodian-Dining Services Dining Services-The Lights Under routine supervision, engage in a variety of housekeeping, custodial and maintenance projects in University buildings and on adjacent grounds. Lead Cook Dining Services-Central Office Under routine supervision, perform and direct others in a variety of duties necessary to lead the preparation of meals and specials in a residential dining operation. Provide skills necessary to lead production areas in residential dining. Supervise the work and maintain service area in a clean, safe and orderly condition. Oversee and prepare a wide variety of soups, sides, salads, entrees, desserts, baked and pastry items; use a variety of kitchen equipment; assist and oversee the kitchen production, ordering and inventory of products, following standardized recipe files; and make recommendations for change/improvement. Sign up for job alerts By signing up for job alerts, you will be notified of vacancies based on your career category selection. You are able to sign up for as many career categories as you would like. Job Alert e0162d1c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Internal Audit/Risk Management Internal Audit/Risk Management Categories Administrative/Professional Other Administrative/Professional Other First Name (required) 1905fb9f Last Name (required) 31d2dc82 Email (required) 4fc9664e Phone Number 39b58002 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673