    "https://jobs.nmu.edu/jobs/food-service-worker-ii-retail-marquette-michigan-united-states-b0b73b5c-10c5-4a5d-afc4-1fef5025c53b": {
      "title": "Food Service Worker II-Retail",
      "description": "Food Service Worker II-Retail - Marquette, Michigan, United States Food Service Worker II-Retail - Marquette, Michigan, United States Skip to Main Content Northern Michigan University Careers Kiosk mode Food Service Worker II-Retail 495194 Marquette, Michigan, 49855 Dining Services-The Lights Staff Closing on: Nov 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Food Service Worker II-Retail Department: Dining Services Term of Assignment: Continuing Term End Date, If Applicable: FLSA Status: Non-Exempt = overtime eligible Work Schedule: Variable shifts/days/locations, including afternoon and weekend shifts; typical work hours are Sunday through Friday, with shift start times between 7:30 am and 1:30 pm. Salary: Hourly rate: $19.15 starting; $20.05 working Travel: No travel Brief Statement of Duties Brief Statement of Duties: Under routine supervision, perform a variety of duties necessary for the daily maintenance, operation and supervision of employees in a retail operation. Provide skills and perform duties in the preparation and resale of various food, beverage and retails items. Ensure success through excellent customer service and maintenance of retail operation standards. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: High School Graduation or Equivalent Required Specialized Training/Certifications: Food Service Sanitation Certification (ServSafe) or the ability to obtain within six months from the start of employment. Required Minimum Work Experience: Eighteen months of experience in retail/convenience store and/or retail restaurant, including cash registers, food preparation, serving, and customer service. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, or Attributes Required for Satisfactory Performance of the Position Duties: Customer and Personal Service-Knowledge of principles and processes for providing customer and personal services. This includes customer needs assessment, meeting quality standards for services, and evaluation of customer satisfaction. Politeness, being courteous, tactful and helpful in dealing with the public and members of the University community. Active Listening-Giving full attention to what other people are saying, taking time to understand the points being made, asking questions as appropriate, and not interrupting at inappropriate times. Instructing-Teaching others how to do something. Speaking-Talking to others to convey information effectively. Service Orientation-Actively looking for ways to help people. Social Perceptiveness-Being aware of others' reactions and understanding why they react as they do. Ability to assess customer orders, kitchen tickets, and expedite food from the kitchen to service team. Oral Comprehension-The ability to listen to and understand information and ideas presented through spoken words and sentences. Manual Dexterity-The ability to quickly move your hand, your hand together with your arm, or your two hands to grasp, manipulate, or assemble objects. Problem Sensitivity-The ability to tell when something is wrong or is likely to go wrong. It does not involve solving the problem, only recognizing there is a problem. The physical capability to perform all of the duties and responsibilities of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Additional Desirable Qualifications Additional Desirable Qualifications: ServSafe Food Service Sanitation Certification. Servsafe Alcohol or TIPS Alcohol Service Certification. Leadership ability demonstrated by experience. Willingness to improve skill level. Special Instructions to Applicants: Submit application, cover letter, resume and references. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Contact Information: Brenda Bickler, Employment Specialist, 906-227-2114 NMU is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now! Recently Posted Jobs Scene Shop Manager Theatre & Dance Responsible for managing the daily operations of the scene shop and supporting the construction and implementation of scenery for all productions within the Department of Theatre & Dance (NMU TD), inclusive of the Wildcat Performing Arts Academy (WPAA). Supervise student workers, additional hired artists, and volunteers while maintaining a safe and professional work environment, and collaborate closely with faculty, staff, and student designers to realize scenic elements for NMU TD & WPAA academic-year and summer productions. Play a vital role in training students in theatrical craftsmanship and shop safety while helping the department maintain efficient and industry-aligned production processes. Production Cook Dining Services-Northern Center Under routine supervision, provide skills and engage in the preparation of food. Prepare a wide variety of soups, salads, entrees, desserts, bakery and pastry items; use a variety of kitchen equipment; follow standardized recipe files; and make recommendations for change/improvement. Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator Internal Audit/Risk Management Manage University records to ensure appropriate access, security, retention, preservation, and disposition in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, and University requirements. Support compliance with digital accessibility standards by assisting employees in creating and maintaining accessible digital records and content. Food Service Worker II-Retail Dining Services-The Lights Under routine supervision, perform a variety of duties necessary for the daily maintenance, operation and supervision of employees in a retail operation. Provide skills and perform duties in the preparation and resale of various food, beverage and retails items. Ensure success through excellent customer service and maintenance of retail operation standards. Custodian-Dining Services Dining Services-The Lights Under routine supervision, engage in a variety of housekeeping, custodial and maintenance projects in University buildings and on adjacent grounds. Lead Cook Dining Services-Central Office Under routine s