      "description": "Director-Accounting Services/Business Manager-Broadcast & AV Services - Marquette, Michigan, United States Director-Accounting Services/Business Manager-Broadcast & AV Services - Marquette, Michigan, United States Skip to Main Content Northern Michigan University Careers Kiosk mode Director-Accounting Services/Business Manager-Broadcast & AV Services 495192 Marquette, Michigan, 49855 Controllers Office Staff Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Director-Accounting Services/Business Manager-Broadcast & AV Services Department: Controller's Office Term of Assignment: Continuing Term End Date, If Applicable: FLSA Status: Exempt = not eligible for overtime Work Schedule: Traditionally Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm with occasional evening and weekend work required. Salary: Targeted salary range: $76,000-$82,000 Travel: Less than 10% Brief Statement of Duties Brief Statement of Duties: Plan, develop, and refine operating procedures and computerized systems for financial reporting. Monitor, review and document University financial transactions for compliance with accounting principles, University policies, federal circulars, and Internal Revenue Service rules and regulations. Prepare and/or assist with preparation of many of the University's financial statements, income tax return, revenue projections of the University endowments and expenditure projections for special projects. Provide senior level accounting and financial expertise to the University's Assistant Controller. Assist the General Manager of WNMU-TV, WNMU-FM, and Audio Visual Services in the fiscal management of these areas. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor's Degree Discipline/Degree Area: Required Specialized Training/Certifications: Required Minimum Work Experience: Five years of recent, progressive experience in accounting, auditing, or finance. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, or Attributes Required for Satisfactory Performance of the Position Duties: Current knowledge of accounting practices and principles. Oral and written communication and comprehension skills. Ability to organize, plan, and prioritize work. Ability to work effectively within a team-base environment. Computer and software application skills. Current knowledge of tax laws. Additional Desirable Qualifications Additional Desirable Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Accounting, Master's Degree in Business and/or CPA certificate. Higher education fund accounting seminars and workshops. Supervisory experience. Other Special Instructions to Applicants: Submit application, cover letter, resume and references. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Contact Information: Erica Jean, HR Generalist, 906-227-1087 NMU is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now! Recently Posted Jobs Scene Shop Manager Theatre & Dance Responsible for managing the daily operations of the scene shop and supporting the construction and implementation of scenery for all productions within the Department of Theatre & Dance (NMU TD), inclusive of the Wildcat Performing Arts Academy (WPAA). Supervise student workers, additional hired artists, and volunteers while maintaining a safe and professional work environment, and collaborate closely with faculty, staff, and student designers to realize scenic elements for NMU TD & WPAA academic-year and summer productions. Play a vital role in training students in theatrical craftsmanship and shop safety while helping the department maintain efficient and industry-aligned production processes. Production Cook Dining Services-Northern Center Under routine supervision, provide skills and engage in the preparation of food. Prepare a wide variety of soups, salads, entrees, desserts, bakery and pastry items; use a variety of kitchen equipment; follow standardized recipe files; and make recommendations for change/improvement. Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator Internal Audit/Risk Managem