    "https://jobs.nmu.edu/jobs/scene-shop-manager-marquette-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Scene Shop Manager",
      "description": "Scene Shop Manager - Marquette, Michigan, United States Scene Shop Manager - Marquette, Michigan, United States Skip to Main Content Northern Michigan University Careers Kiosk mode Scene Shop Manager 495178 Marquette, Michigan, 49855 Theatre & Dance Staff Closing on: Nov 10 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Scene Shop Manager Department: Theatre & Dance Term of Assignment: Term Term End Date, If Applicable: December 20, 2028 FLSA Status: Non-Exempt = overtime eligible Work Schedule: Traditionally Monday-Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm with occasional evening and weekend work required. Salary: Targeted Salary Range: $40,160-$43,100 Travel: Less than 10% Brief Statement of Duties Brief Statement of Duties: Responsible for managing the daily operations of the scene shop and supporting the construction and implementation of scenery for all productions within the Department of Theatre & Dance (NMU TD), inclusive of the Wildcat Performing Arts Academy (WPAA). Supervise student workers, additional hired artists, and volunteers while maintaining a safe and professional work environment, and collaborate closely with faculty, staff, and student designers to realize scenic elements for NMU TD & WPAA academic-year and summer productions. Play a vital role in training students in theatrical craftsmanship and shop safety while helping the department maintain efficient and industry-aligned production processes. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor's Degree Discipline/Degree Area: Required Specialized Training/Certifications: Required Minimum Work Experience: One year of carpentry and/or scenic construction experience. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, or Attributes Required for Satisfactory Performance of the Position Duties: Working knowledge of theatre and scene shop safety practices. Proficiency in scenic construction techniques, including wood and metalwork. Familiarity with safe operation of power tools, pneumatic tools, and welding equipment. Strong organizational, time management, and interpersonal communication skills. Adaptability and creative problem solving skills. Additional Desirable Qualifications Additional Desirable Qualifications: Degree in Theatre, Technical Production, or a related field. Experience teaching undergraduate classes. Experience mentoring and supervising student crews in a production or academic environment. Experience collaborating with production staff in an educational or professional theatre setting. Knowledge of working drawings and theatrical rigging. Prior involvement in youth or educational arts programming. Other Special Instructions to Applicants: Submit application, cover letter, resume and references. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Contact Information: Erica Jean, HR Generalist, 906-227-1087 NMU is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now! Recently Posted Jobs Food Service Worker II-Retail Dining Services-The Lights Under routine supervision, perform a variety of duties necessary for the daily maintenance, operation and supervision of employees in a retail operation. Provide skills and perform duties in the preparation and resale of various food, beverage and retails items. Ensure success through excellent customer service and maintenance of retail operation standards. Scene Shop Manager Theatre & Dance Responsible for managing the daily operations of the scene shop and supporting the construction and implementation of scenery for all productions within the Department of Theatre & Dance (NMU TD), inclusive of the Wildcat Performing Arts Academy (WPAA). Supervise student workers, additional hired artists, and volunteers while maintaining a safe and professional work environment, and collaborate closely with faculty, staff, and student designers to realize scenic elements for NMU TD & WPAA academic-year and summer productions. Play a vital role in training students in theatrical craftsmanship and shop safety while helping the department maintain efficient and industry-aligned production processes. Production Cook Dining Services-Northern Center Under routine supervision, provide skills and engage in the preparation of food. Prepare a wide variety of soups, salads, entrees, desserts, bakery and pastry items; use a variety of kitchen equipment; follow standardized recipe files; and make recommendations for change/improvement. Records Management & Digital Accessibility Coordinator Internal Audit/Risk Management Manage University records to ensure appropriate access, security, retention, preservation, and disposition in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, and University requirements. Support compliance with digital accessibility standards by assisting employees in creating and maintaining accessible digital records and content. Custodian-Dining Services Dining Services-The Lights Under routine supervision, engage in a variety of housekeeping, custodial and maintenance projects in University buildings and on adjacent grounds. Lead Cook Dining Services-Central Office Under routine supervision, perform and direct others in a variety of duties necessary to lead the preparation of meals and specials in a residential dining operation. Provide skills necessary to lead production areas in residential dining. Supervise the work and maintain service area in a clean, safe and orderly condition. Oversee and prepare a wide variety of soups, sides, salads, entrees, desserts, baked and pastry items; use a variety of kitchen equipment; assist and oversee the kitchen production, ordering and inventory of products, following standardized recipe files; and make recommendations for change/improvement. Sign up for job alerts By signing up for job alerts, you will be notified of vacancies based on your career category selection. You are able to sign up for as many career categories as you would like. Job Alert 88559f5b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select